(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #111. Each element of a list literal is copied
 independently, so `[inner, inner]` produces TWO separate copies, not one
 shared pointer duplicated - reading each slot out and mutating one must
 not affect the other or the original.)

a list called inner is [1, 2].
a list called outer is [inner, inner].
a list called first_elem is element 1 of outer.
a list called second_elem is element 2 of outer.
Set element 1 of first_elem to 999.
print first_elem.
print second_elem.
print inner.
